sec.p:
According to ABCBio (ABCBio n.d.), “biological control” refers to the use of organisms or natural substances produced by organisms to prevent, reduce, or eradicate pest and disease outbreaks. Products are commonly grouped as:
Macro-organisms (insects, mites, nematodes that parasitize or prey on pests);
Microorganisms (bacteria, fungi, viruses that infect pests);
Biochemicals (plant/algal extracts, enzymes, hormones that can induce plant resistance); and
Semiochemicals (pheromones and related metabolites used for monitoring, mass trapping, and mating disruption).
